t offers sandwich insulated panels, such as polyurethane foam/PIR, expanded polystyrene, rockwool, and glass wool panels; pre-engineered steel buildings, such as multi-storey and warehouse buildings, industrial shed, factory buildings, and cold storage buildings; pre-fabricated structures, including pre-fab site offices, control rooms, railway shelters, labour hutments, pre-fabricated housing, low-cost housing, acoustic enclosures, and portable security guard cabins; Light Gauge Steel Framing for roofs, floors, walls, or entire buildings; and pre-fabricated structures and its components; standard modular solutions comprising porta and liftable cabins, Mi homes, and modular housing solutions; EPS (Expanded Polystyrene) Packaging provides expanded polystyrene (EPS) shape molding products for protective packaging, custom insulation solutions, and specialized industrial applications; and EPS block molding products for use in construction, packaging, and insulation applications. It serves industrial sectors, including general engineering and manufacturing, food and beverages, warehousing and logistics, power, textiles, and railways. The company was formerly known as E-Pack Polymers Private Limited and changed its name to EPack Prefab Technologies Limited in December 2024. The company was incorporated in 1999 and is based in Greater Noida, India.","employees":2671,"earnDates":[],"exDiv":null,"asOf":1795774612},"analyst":{"key":null,"mean":null,"n":2,"tMean":275,"tHigh":280,"tLow":270,"tMed":275,"currency":"INR","asOf":1795774612,"trend":{"strongBuy":0,"buy":2,"hold":0,"sell":0,"strongSell":0}},"cap":"Other","caFix":null,"fetched":1795774612,"source":"Yahoo Finance (public chart, fundamentals-timeseries & quoteSummary endpoints)","news":{"q":"\"EPack Prefab Technologies\" when:90d","items":[{"t":"EPack Prefab Technologies (NSEI:EPACKPEB) - Stock Analysis","s":"Simply Wall St","d":1795507200,"u":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikAFBVV95cUxNMG1BNnJ1QXluWm9uWlFXbGFGa